        section("Effects and constraints",
            "`create_at(address, bytes)` requires a nonnull page-aligned address, including when the request is zero. A nonzero request maps a page-rounded extent at that exact address, rejects a different returned address, and registers fixed external provenance. Its returned chunk length is the requested byte count, rather than the whole page-rounded mapping.",
            "`destroy(chunk)` reconstructs the page-rounded mapping length, unregisters provenance, and unmaps the mapping. The supplied chunk must match the original address and logical length. No existing mapping is intentionally replaced, and object lifetimes are not managed."),
